    },
    "body": "The previous coupled pass left six conditional errors and repeatedly broke one protected guard when EOS improved. This adds a host-only Rust analyzer using the existing native factor API and records complete original/final saved-population incidence, so the next learning change can be based on actual shared coefficients.\n\nThe seven EOS vetoes are one unary coordinate at one incumbent epoch. Eight pair directions avoid that particular signed conflict, but fifteen unary directions do too. The relevant new observation is narrower pair sharing: pair51817 touches117 original guard/token incidences with zero required-winner hits, versus380 guard frames and12969 token incidences for its unary937 component. This supports a bounded generic pair-credit question; it does not prove unary inseparability, legal-code/full-pool feasibility or improved language behavior. Accepted8/512 and conditional9/15 are unchanged.\n\nValidation at exact head aef72eb28: four focused Rust example tests; optimized offline/locked build; actual native enumeration of all4096 tokens in391 original and391 final states; all391 original states validated through frozen bridge transport; input and output full-file Rust seals; named formatting and claim wording. Exact-source self-review plus independent mathematical interpretation review are retained. Buffered9.0334s and unbuffered308.7714s reports have exactly equal scientific contents, excluding elapsed time/output path. No new model, gradients, proposals or autoregressive run.\n\nBoth complete reports, the superseded reader patch/INDEX, source/runtime identities, iCloud round-trip receipts and cumulative costs are preserved. After protected merge, verify all26 delivered paths on fresh main, remove the remote/local branch and owned worktree, clear temporary inputs/build files and run the current hygiene tool. No pod was provisioned.\n\nReferences #2030. Does not close the milestone or adopt its proposed acceptance thresholds.\n",
